{
  "publication_number": "CN117875447A",
  "title": "FPGA acceleration scheme for federally learning Paillier algorithm",
  "assignee": "Hefei University of Technology",
  "filing_date": "2023-12-29",
  "publication_date": "2024-04-12",
  "pse": {
    "problem": "The traditional federated learning direction requires a lot of computing power for neural network reasoning and Paillier encryption algorithm, introducing significant overheads that can be compensated by dedicated circuits.",
    "solution_function": "The invention optimizes the Montgomery large number modular multiplication algorithm to improve division operation efficiency in binary chips, replacing it with a process using displacement, multiplication, and other processes. This improves FPGA's computing efficiency and speed for the Paillier algorithm.",
    "solution_structure": "The solution uses an Ethernet interface for high-speed data transmission between the host and FPGA, FIFO as a cache for data input and output, and C language to improve the Montgomery modular multiplication algorithm and combine it with the large number Karatsuba algorithm.",
    "solution_implementation": "Data is transmitted quickly from the host system to the FPGA to meet GPU parallel computing requirements using an Ethernet interface. FIFO is used as a cache for data input and output. The improved Montgomery modular multiplication algorithm is implemented using C language and combined with the large number Karatsuba algorithm.",
    "effect": "The solution provides computing power support for its encryption algorithm, improving efficiency and reducing GOU computing power costs."
  },
